{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment5.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `_signOut` has no error handling or in-flight guard**

```dart
Future<void> _signOut() async {
  await authService.signOut();
  onSignedOut?.call();
}
```

If `signOut()` throws (e.g. the store/plugin call fails), the future rejects
unhandled: no feedback, user stays on Home. Also, a double-tap runs it twice.
Consider guarding and reporting:

```dart
bool _signingOut = false;

Future<void> _signOut() async {
  if (_signingOut) return;
  _signingOut = true;
  try {
    await authService.signOut();
    onSignedOut?.call();
  } catch (_) {
    if (context.mounted) {
      ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
        const SnackBar(content: Text('Sign out failed. Please try again.')),
      );
    }
  } finally {
    _signingOut = false;
  }
}
```

Low risk today (`DefaultAuthGateway.signOut` swallows Google errors), but the UI layer
should not rely on every gateway implementation being failure-free.
"}

